Hi, 
here is the original PCformat app which !PCconfig uses. It could do with
a spruce up to look a bit more style-guide compliant, and also to give drive
sizes in 'RISCOS MB' as well as 'DOS MB (million bytes)'. Not defaulting to
10Mb might be a good idea too...

If you want to get nerdy and learn about partition formats then a choice of
FAT type (16-bit 32-bit etc) is also on the cards. It also needs testing with
massive hard discs, but I don't suppose you have one of those either?

I can do this stuff, but it fits quite well with the PCconfig stuff you are
doing so I'll let you have first refusal...

Wookey
